<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Albert of Sardinia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1849</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Albert was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1831. In 1848 he granted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statuto-albertino">Statuto Albertino</a>, a constitution that later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s, and declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in support of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> revolt. Defeated at Custoza in 1848 and Novara in 1849, he abdicated in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a> and died in exile in Portugal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-albert-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="Charles Albert of Sardinia" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ferdinando Cavalleri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlo_Alberto_by_Cavalleri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
